Z||000012||Tonker||11-08-2001||11:27 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Mach10:<BR><B>  <BR>Liberals: Well rounded, and realistic<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><B>AHAHAHAHAHAHAHAHAHAHAHA!!!!</B> Ahem, I'm sorry. Don't know where that came from...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_wtf.gif"><BR>You mean the same Liberals that scrapped an order to replace our outdated and dangerous Sea King helicopters with EH 101s(I don't even remember how much money we lost on that one), only then to decide that we do indeed need to get new Helos, but then decided that we should wait longer to order new Helos because the requirements put forth by the Department of National Defence too closely matched the specs for the Helos that the Liberals originally scrapped?(*takes a deep breath*) Or would it be, instead, the "other" Liberals that unseated the Tories with promises to get rid of the much hated GST, against which they had been railing for the past several years and had openly and vehemently opposed in the election only to go back on their promise after the election? Perhaps you're referring to the Liberals that have cut defense spending so far that we can no longer contribute in any meaningful way to the action in Afhganistan and seriously degrades our ability to maintain our NATO and peacekeeping committments?<P>Face it Jean Chretien and the Liberals are as cretinous as as the other parties we have. If they were still around, I'd vote Rhino party. Maybe I'll vote NDP next time to see how bad they can fück up our country...||||reg||13
Z||000013||Mach10||11-08-2001||11:37 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Tonker:<BR><B> [b]AHAHAHAHAHAHAHAHAHAHAHA!!!!</B> Ahem, I'm sorry. Don't know where that came from...   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_wtf.gif"> <BR>You mean the same Liberals that scrapped an order to replace our outdated and dangerous Sea King helicopters with EH 101s(I don't even remember how much money we lost on that one), only then to decide that we do indeed need to get new Helos, but then decided that we should wait longer to order new Helos because the requirements put forth by the Department of National Defence too closely matched the specs for the Helos that the Liberals originally scrapped?(*takes a deep breath*) Or would it be, instead, the "other" Liberals that unseated the Tories with promises to get rid of the much hated GST, against which they had been railing for the past several years and had openly and vehemently opposed in the election only to go back on their promise after the election? Perhaps you're referring to the Liberals that have cut defense spending so far that we can no longer contribute in any meaningful way to the action in Afhganistan and seriously degrades our ability to maintain our NATO and peacekeeping committments?<P>Face it Jean Chretien and the Liberals are as cretinous as as the other parties we have. If they were still around, I'd vote Rhino party. Maybe I'll vote NDP next time to see how bad they can fück up our country...[/B]<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>hehehe... He's kinda got a point... But let's face it... Jean Cretin (sic) is the best we got. Can you imagine STOCKWELL DAY at the helm?<P>On the other hand, I likes the liberal party JUST fine. Yeah, there's been fnck-ups... Show me a party that doesn't. Just 'cos the liberals haven't axed the GST? Well, we're pretty much in the green now. Spending is getting better. I don't think that pulling the money back out will do our budget much good. I was refering to the GST's inception. At that time, the money was misdirected god-knows-where. Now, on the other hand, the Liberals actually had our economy moving somewhat... After years of funding cuts, the Liberals are starting to move money back into health and education... <BR>So what are you complaining about?||||reg||10
Z||000014||Tonker||11-09-2001||06:49 PM||||Actually Mach I disagree with your point abouth the Liberals getting the economy moving. They contributed, but a lot of the recovery is attributed to the foundation laid by the Tories in their last term. The recession of the 80's can be traced back to the Grits.<P>I don't think anything our government does affects the economy in a meaningful way. Our economy is more strongly affected by the actions of the US government. Our government can moderate the economic climate to a certain extent, but if the US economy goes down so does ours.<P>Now lest you think that I'm supporting the Tories, I'm not. I don't support any particular party, but I would like to see the Conservatives give Jean and his cronies a kick in the ass next election. The Libs have been in power for too long, they've forgotten what got them there in the first place, and they're now suffering from the same arrogance that they critiqued in the Tories. <P>||||reg||1
Z||000015||BN Boomer||11-09-2001||11:05 PM||||Sorry, but judging strictly by outcome and results, your "Liberal" party does indeed appear to be very close to our "Liberal" party, the Democrats. After all, it was your f*cked up health care system that Hillary wanted to pattern one for us after. Our Democrats seek to emulate Canadian gun control laws. <P>You can play semantics all you want (Our most popular and famous recent Democrat likes to play with them as well), but there ain't no escaping the truth.||||reg||1
Z||000016||Mach10||11-10-2001||03:38 AM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by BN Boomer:<BR><B>Sorry, but judging strictly by outcome and results, your "Liberal" party does indeed appear to be very close to our "Liberal" party, the Democrats. After all, it was your f*cked up health care system that Hillary wanted to pattern one for us after. Our Democrats seek to emulate Canadian gun control laws. <P>You can play semantics all you want (Our most popular and famous recent Democrat likes to play with them as well), but there ain't no escaping the truth.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>****ed up health-care, huh? How much did YOU pay for your MRI? Ultrasound? Broken leg? Shattered rib? Broken ankle? 12-time chronic asthma episode? <BR>I didn't pay **** , didn't wait longer than a week... Sorry, what's ****ed up? Or is the HMO system the proper way to do it? Swipe a VISA before starting CPR? 3 options for Emerg? Coach, Business, First Class? Champagne drips for the rich, recycled needles for the poor? Very effective poverty control: Ensure that all the poor people can't afford doctors, then let natural selection do the rest... Don't make me laugh. <BR>The Tories (right-wing) have ****ed this country over so many times... It's only now that things are starting to be put right. I vote Liberal, and until someone gives me a damn good reason why I shouldn't I'll stay that way. JC has done more for this country than ANY ONE of our past leaders, with the possible exception of Pierre Trudeau. But I forgot, winning 3 straight elections doesn't count for JACK, does it? Neither do results? The Liberal party is doing JUST FINE. Especially when you consider the opposition... <P>Gun Control rules. Give me a perfectly good reason why EVERYONE has the RIGHT to a firearm. C'mon, try me. King George after you guys again? Can't think of any other way to solve your social problems? Society so ****ed up that the police can't help you? Yup, guns are a necessary part of life, ain't they?<P>EDIT: <BR>You know what? Forget it. I don't presume to comment on your government, because I don't have a fncking clue what I'm talking about. I suggest you do the same. The only thing that YOU'VE ever seen was what your party-friendly media is gouting at you. I get American stations. I see what's going on. How many Canadian feeds do you get? What do you know about our country? Our government? Our Healthcare system? You are told whatever makes the paying party look the best. Your media is mocked GLOBALLY because it's so PITIFULLY obvious... How is it that you can't even see it?. God forbid that your HMO system should look bad because us Cannucks are doing it the right way? *gasp*<p>[This message has been edited by Mach10 (edited 11-10-2001).]||||reg||4
Z||000017||Mach10||11-10-2001||04:01 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Tonker:<BR><B>Actually Mach I disagree with your point abouth the Liberals getting the economy moving. They contributed, but a lot of the recovery is attributed to the foundation laid by the Tories in their last term. The recession of the 80's can be traced back to the Grits.<P>I don't think anything our government does affects the economy in a meaningful way. Our economy is more strongly affected by the actions of the US government. Our government can moderate the economic climate to a certain extent, but if the US economy goes down so does ours.<P>Now lest you think that I'm supporting the Tories, I'm not. I don't support any particular party, but I would like to see the Conservatives give Jean and his cronies a kick in the ass next election. The Libs have been in power for too long, they've forgotten what got them there in the first place, and they're now suffering from the same arrogance that they critiqued in the Tories. <P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>I have to admit that this is true. Yes, the Libs have been in a little too long. We need some fresh new parties... Unfortunately, look what we're stuck with. I don't think the Cons would be very constructive at all. They haven't been in the past, and certainly aren't doing much good where they ARE in power. We just tossed them out of MB, and all they have been doing is whining about how the NDP is fncking up... Funny, it's THEIR mess that they are trying (unsuccessfully, I'm not pleased with NDP performance so far) to clean up...<P>The only viable alternatives, with a good vote-share are the Alliance party. Not a bad premise, but there is a genetics lab looking for some stray test-patients. There are FAR too many chromasomes in THAT party. Can 'em all, (including Doris) and start from scratch. Maybe they might have something meaningful to say. Probably not  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif"><P>As far as the economics go, my choice of wording was wrong. You are right. The economy pretty much does it's own thing. My focus was on spending/budget/surplus/deficit<BR>The liberals, although some "trimming" was done in their early terms, they are starting to dump money back into the programs that the people want. I've had $900 knocked off my tuition. Hospitals are getting equipment/nurses. Things are looking up, even as our dollar slips lower  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif"><BR>||||reg||6
