Z||000022||JohnnyK||11-11-2001||05:10 PM||||****ed up health care eh? hahahha.. I'm sorry, I have to join in on the laughing at this one. I have a question though, if an american comes to canada and breaks his neck, does he get care? I would assume he does. Whenever I drive down to the states, I have to buy stinking health insurance.<P>Anyways, I agree that gun control is a stupid, stupid thing, and thats part of the reason I liked Alliance, till I realized he was nuts..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000023||BN Boomer||11-12-2001||01:54 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Mach10:<BR><B>  ****ed up health-care, huh? How much did YOU pay for your MRI? Ultrasound? Broken leg? Shattered rib? Broken ankle? 12-time chronic asthma episode? <BR>I didn't pay **** , didn't wait longer than a week... Sorry, what's ****ed up? Or is the HMO system the proper way to do it? Swipe a VISA before starting CPR? 3 options for Emerg? Coach, Business, First Class? Champagne drips for the rich, recycled needles for the poor? Very effective poverty control: Ensure that all the poor people can't afford doctors, then let natural selection do the rest... Don't make me laugh. <BR>The Tories (right-wing) have ****ed this country over so many times... It's only now that things are starting to be put right. I vote Liberal, and until someone gives me a damn good reason why I shouldn't I'll stay that way. JC has done more for this country than ANY ONE of our past leaders, with the possible exception of Pierre Trudeau. But I forgot, winning 3 straight elections doesn't count for JACK, does it? Neither do results? The Liberal party is doing JUST FINE. Especially when you consider the opposition... <P>Gun Control rules. Give me a perfectly good reason why EVERYONE has the RIGHT to a firearm. C'mon, try me. King George after you guys again? Can't think of any other way to solve your social problems? Society so ****ed up that the police can't help you? Yup, guns are a necessary part of life, ain't they?<P>EDIT: <BR>You know what? Forget it. I don't presume to comment on your government, because I don't have a fncking clue what I'm talking about. I suggest you do the same. The only thing that YOU'VE ever seen was what your party-friendly media is gouting at you. I get American stations. I see what's going on. How many Canadian feeds do you get? What do you know about our country? Our government? Our Healthcare system? You are told whatever makes the paying party look the best. Your media is mocked GLOBALLY because it's so PITIFULLY obvious... How is it that you can't even see it?. God forbid that your HMO system should look bad because us Cannucks are doing it the right way? *gasp*<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I don't live very far from the border. (Yup, even get Canadian feeds, moron) My job also takes me up into Vancouver, BC. Your arguments obviously explain why so many doctors offices and medical clinics around here are clogged up with Canadians trying to get timely health care. And how financially sound is your health care? Oh, that's right, they just raise your taxes a little bit more to cover it. Why don't you just give your whole paycheck to your government so they can wipe your a$$ for the rest of your life? <P>I don't need or want some nanny government babysitting me from birth to grave. If you are such a lacky that is unable to take care of yourself and are totally dependent on such a sytem, be grateful for being born Canada.<P>You obviously do not understand or appreciate freedom. No one should have to explain to you or anyone why they want to own a gun. It's called freedom, you twit. Something that is obviously dwindling quickly in Canada. Maybe you should have to explain why you want to own something as dangerous as a vehicle that is capable of exceeding legal speed limits by such a large degree. Remember, cars still kill a lot more than guns. Yup, fast cars are a necessary part of life, ain't they? I'd suggest that you buy a clue, but with your poor economy and pathetic exchange rate, you probably can't afford one.<BR>||||reg||1
